---
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';

const retrieveUsername = 'https://uk.godaddy.com/help/i-forgot-my-username-19121';
const accountRecovery = 'https://supportcenter.godaddy.com/accountrecovery';
const recoveryHelp = 'https://www.godaddy.com/help/regain-access-to-my-domain-or-my-godaddy-account-4043';
const godaddyPhone = '020 7084 1810';
const godaddyTel = '+442070841810';
---

<Layout
  title="Domain recovery | Bankside MOT & Repair"
  description="How to recover the GoDaddy account for banksidemot.co.uk so the new workshop website can go live."
  noindex
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Domain recovery', path: '/domain-recovery' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="bg-slate-50 py-12">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <div>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-brand-100 bg-brand-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-brand-600 uppercase">For Colin — not a customer page</span>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">Recover banksidemot.co.uk</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700">
          You are not stuck. The domain is still on GoDaddy until February 2027. Once we are into that account, we point it at the new site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">What we already know</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Domain: <strong class="text-slate-900">banksidemot.co.uk</strong></li>
          <li>Registrar: <strong class="text-slate-900">GoDaddy</strong></li>
          <li>Registered: 14 February 2024 · Expires: <strong class="text-slate-900">14 February 2027</strong></li>
          <li>The old website is still live on that name. That is fine for now.</li>
          <li>Gordon bought it for the garage. You believe it is <strong class="text-slate-900">your</strong> GoDaddy account, in your name.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Gordon going quiet only matters if the domain sits in <em>his</em> login. If it is yours, we recover it without him.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Do this in order</h2>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-brand-600 uppercase">Step 1 — 10 minutes</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Find the username</h3>
          <p>
            Go to GoDaddy’s
            <a href={retrieveUsername} class="font-semibold text-brand-700 underline decoration-brand-200 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-800" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">forgot username page</a>
            and try every email you actually use:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Your personal email (Gmail, Outlook, etc.)</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900">sales@forthcarz.co.uk</span></li>
            <li>Any other Forth Carz or Bankside address</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When it asks for a domain, type <strong class="text-slate-900">banksidemot.co.uk</strong>. If a code arrives, you are in the right place — then
            <a href="https://uk.godaddy.com/help/reset-my-password-356" class="font-semibold text-brand-700 underline decoration-brand-200 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-800" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reset the password</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-brand-600 uppercase">Step 2 — if step 1 fails</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Phone GoDaddy</h3>
          <p>They are used to this. Call from a quiet room with this page open.</p>
          <p>
            <a href={`tel:${godaddyTel}`} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-brand-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-brand-700">
              Call GoDaddy UK {godaddyPhone}
            </a>
          </p>
          <p>24/7. Say:</p>
          <blockquote class="rounded-xl border border-slate-100 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3 text-slate-800">
            “I’ve lost the username and password for my GoDaddy account. The domain is banksidemot.co.uk. I am the owner. I need to recover the account.”
          </blockquote>
          <p>Jeremie can sit on the call if that helps.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-brand-600 uppercase">Step 3 — if they ask for paperwork</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Account recovery form</h3>
          <p>
            Use
            <a href={accountRecovery} class="font-semibold text-brand-700 underline decoration-brand-200 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-800" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GoDaddy account recovery</a>
            and choose <strong class="text-slate-900">Domain Access</strong> (you are the owner, but you cannot get into the account).
          </p>
          <p>
            Full steps:
            <a href={recoveryHelp} class="font-semibold text-brand-700 underline decoration-brand-200 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-800" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Regain access to my domain or GoDaddy account</a>.
          </p>
          <p>You will need a colour photo of photo ID in the <strong class="text-slate-900">same name</strong> as the domain owner — driving licence is fine. Have it ready before you start.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Have this to hand</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Domain: <strong class="text-slate-900">banksidemot.co.uk</strong></li>
          <li>Workshop: {business.streetAddress}, {business.addressLocality} {business.postalCode}</li>
          <li>Garage phone: {business.telephoneDisplay}</li>
          <li>Driving licence or passport</li>
          <li>A list of emails to try</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">If it turns out to be Gordon’s login</h2>
        <p>
          Then GoDaddy will treat it as his account. We do not fight that. Plan B is a new domain, and we can move later if the original comes back. Do not start that until we know step 1–3 have failed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
        This page is only for recovering the domain so the new Bankside site can go live. It is not linked from the customer menu.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
